# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish these: local cracking artefacts contain handshakes and cracked
# passwords of other people's networks, and the client/cracker are third-party
# downloads (help_crack.py is GPL-3.0+, hashcat is MIT).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# the dwpa client itself, and everything it writes into its working directory
# (.res .hash .key .rules .challenge.dict .restore .pid .induct* .outfiles*)
help_crack.*

# cracker session state, for any --session name
*.restore
*.pid
*.potfile
*.induct
*.induct.*
inducts/
*.outfiles/
*.hcstat2

# handshakes and cracker artefacts, whatever the session name or format: a stray
# capture in the repo would publish someone's network
*.cap
*.cap.gz
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.22000
*.hc22000
*.pmkid
*.hash
*.key
*.res

# dictionaries downloaded / extracted by the client
cracked.txt
cracked.txt.gz
wpskey*.txt
wpskey*.txt.gz
prdict.txt
prdict.txt.gz

# bundled cracker (install it yourself, see dashboard/README.md)
hashcat/
hashcat-*/
hashcat*.7z
hashcat*.zip
JohnTheRipper/
john-*/

# dashboard runtime state: settings may hold a site key, keys.jsonl holds
# cracked passwords, session.log holds the client's output
dashboard/settings.json
dashboard/keys.jsonl
dashboard/geo.json
dashboard/world.json
dashboard/land.json
dashboard/coast.json
dashboard/session.log
dashboard/session.log.1
*.tmp

# secrets, if you ever add any
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# os / editor noise and patch leftovers
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
*.orig
*.rej

# local-only Android shell (WebView around the dashboard, installed over adb).
# A personal build, not part of the published project: keep it out of git.
android/
